{0 Routing primitives}

{!Httpkit_router} matches methods and raw origin-form paths against a bounded,
declaration-ordered table. Patterns support literals, named parameters and a
final wildcard. The table stores application data without invoking handlers.

Query strings do not affect matching. Percent escapes, case, dot segments and
repeated slashes retain their exact spelling. Captures remain encoded bytes.
A caller must choose decoding, authorization and filesystem policies explicitly.

A method mismatch returns the distinct matching methods, allowing an application
to choose its 405 response and Allow header. HEAD and OPTIONS are not synthesized.
